<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Deletion gate has zero coverage for the generic envelope wire codec construct family" ;
  triage:description "AI.11 sprint doc requires deletion gate test to reject six construct families: pipe, Windows AF_UNIX, generic envelope wire codec, duplicate router, non-loopback bind, and adapter storage/nudge calls. Test ai11_deletion_gate_rejects_retired_windows_transport_ast_and_dependencies() covers five families (pipe/AF_UNIX, non-loopback bind, duplicate router, adapter storage/nudge calls) but has zero test coverage for the retired generic HTTP RequestEnvelope/ResponseEnvelope wire-codec pattern. No active production violation exists; risk is purely the gate's inability to catch future regression reintroducing the generic envelope codec." ;
  triage:category "test-coverage-gap" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE/s11/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s12/b6466aa1> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/bb20fd9a> ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "feature/pAI-s12-post-write-router" ;
  triage:notes "RESOLUTION (2026-07-22 sweep): verifiably fixed on current integrate/phase-AI. A dedicated test, fn ai11_deletion_gate_detector_rejects_retired_envelope_wire_codec_ast_fixtures() (boundary_enforcement.rs ~line 478), now covers the retired generic HTTP RequestEnvelope/ResponseEnvelope wire-codec construct family that this finding identified as missing. Cross-referenced with sibling finding AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST.ttl (same cwin fast-follow batch, PR #607), already recorded fixed on feature/pAI-s12-post-write-router (b6466aa1); this finding's fix landed in the same batch." .

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA7-ATM-QA-201-ENVELOPE-CODEC-COVERAGE>
  triage:assignedTo "cwin" ;
  triage:dispatchChannel "direct-paste-non-atm" ;
  triage:notes "ASSIGNMENT UPDATE (team-lead, 2026-07-22): the AI.11 QA-7 fast-follow batch (this finding plus AI11-QA7-ARCH-001-HARDCODED-ALLOWLIST and AI11-QA7-ARCH-002-TAUTOLOGICAL-DUPLICATE-CHECK) was reassigned from arch-ctm to cwin. Original ATM dispatch was message 01KY5PZ9PCJMZP3ZFA92NGCGS5 (task id AI11-QA7-FASTFOLLOW-DELETION-GATE-SCOPE, sent to arch-ctm). arch-ctm was subsequently stood down from this batch via ATM message 01KY5S0ZFQCPA89KD5WTM0Z6CA. cwin has no ATM identity, so the reassignment dispatch to cwin was delivered by direct-paste outside the ATM channel and left no ATM message trail on cwin's side; the stand-down message to arch-ctm is the only ATM-side record of the handoff. This note is the canonical audit trail for the reassignment." .

